<!--
  DRUM_LURE_PREDATOR_BUILD_1. deep_desert.md §4's actual named archetype —
  "the ground lies to you": predators hunt by vibration and appraise by
  water, and "some carry lures that drum juicy — an angler's decoy that
  sounds like a fat animal." RSW_SandLion (EXTREME_DESERT_SUBSURFACE_
  PREDATOR_1) is a straight ambush predator filling the biome's icon role
  in the interim; this is the deeper mechanic the item asked for, a
  distinct creature, not a re-skin of the sand lion. Do not touch
  RSW_SandLion's own wiring.

  drazzik: DRAFTED pseudo-Star-Wars name (NONCANON_BEAST_RENAME_1 process —
  agent drafts, owner reacts), checked against check_pseudo_sw_name.py
  (PASS: 2 syllables, doubled letter, k-ending, no canon collision, no
  English stem). Not yet owner-ruled.

  MECHANIC 1 — the lure (RM_CompProperties_DrumLure, RimMandrake.
  CreatureBehaviors, this item's own new C#). Confirmed before writing any
  C#: no stock RimWorld comp broadcasts a false signal that pulls another
  pawn's own pathing toward a tile (rimsage search_defs/search_source for
  "Lure" — zero hits in vanilla+DLC; this codebase's own two nearest
  sibling ambush mechanisms, CompProperties_AquaticAmbusher and
  RM_CompProperties_HeatBurstPredator, only ever act on the predator, never
  compel the victim). See RM_CompDrumLure's own header for the state
  machine. luredHediff/submersionHediff point at the two generic hediffs in
  RM_DrumLure_Hediffs.xml (RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors, sibling to that
  assembly's own RM_AquaticAmbush_Hediffs.xml). No MayRequire on the comp
  Class itself: RSW_WraidAlpha (this mod, DESERT_BURST_PREDATOR_FLAGSHIP_1)
  already references RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_CompProperties_
  HeatBurstPredator the same way, unguarded — this mod already treats that
  assembly as a hard dependency in practice (loadAfter mandrake.rm.
  creaturebehaviors, this file's own About.xml).

  MECHANIC 2 — the egg-trap clutch (deep_desert.md §4 "eggs are canteens —
  and some are traps... the newborn tries to drink the intruder... sharp
  beaks and needle claws... the clutch is bait"). Built as an ordinary
  vanilla CompProperties_EggLayer clutch below (RSW_DrazzikEggFertilized/
  Unfertilized), same shape as this mod's own RSW_WraidAlpha eggs and
  RSW_BrainWormEggCluster (BrainWorms, absorbed pattern) — a mother that
  invests water in a weapon, per the sheet's own line, rather than an
  invented spawner building. The fertilized egg carries the exact same
  RimMandrake.ProximityHatch.CompProperties_ProximityHatch already proven
  live in this mod (RSW_ProtovermesEgg_ProximityHatch.xml, Patches/
  ProximityHatch) and in BrainWorms' RSW_BrainWormEggCluster — MayRequire-
  gated, so without that mod the clutch just falls back to CompHatcher's
  vanilla timer.

  Reading "interacted with (hauled/picked up)" (item prose) as PROXIMITY
  rather than a haul-hook: deep_desert.md §4 itself says "Approached, they
  hatch violently" — proximity is the sheet's own wording, closer to it
  than inventing a haul-interrupt comp would be, and it reuses C# already
  shipped and tested rather than adding a second new mechanism. Specs state
  outcomes (rimworld-modding skill / FOUNDRY doctrine); this is the better
  route while the criteria (reads as water, hatches hostile on approach) is
  met.

  BODY/ART: reuses RSW_SandLion's own body shape (QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail)
  and donor texture, TEMP PLACEHOLDER, tinted pale bone/dust per deep_desert.md
  §9's palette ("bleached bone, pale dust... no green, no black char") to read
  as visually distinct from the untinted sand lion despite the shared
  silhouette — same reskin-over-shared-art idiom this mod's own RSW_WraidAlpha
  uses over RSW_Wraid. Checked infrastructure/artpipe/done/, _artsrc/ and
  registry.jsonl for "drazzik"/"drum"/"lure" before placeholder-reusing: none
  found (new name, first mention this session) — a real render remains owed,
  not commissioned this pass.

  Wired into RUT_ExtremeDesert at LOW commonality (0.05, a tenth of
  RSW_SandLion's 0.5) per the item's own "rare, dangerous encounter, not a
  common spawn" instruction and the sheet's §5/§6 population bans.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RSW_Drazzik</defName>
    <label>drazzik</label>
    <description>A pale, patient thing that lies still beneath the sand for hours, humming a false vibration through the ground that sounds exactly like something fat and wounded. Whatever comes to investigate walks the rest of the way in on its own. By the time the drazzik surfaces, the strike is already decided — the appraisal happened while it was still hidden.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>5.5</MoveSpeed>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>100</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <MarketValue>700</MarketValue>
      <FilthRate>2</FilthRate>
      <Wildness>0.95</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>left claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>16</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.5</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <surpriseAttack>
          <extraMeleeDamages>
            <li>
              <def>Stun</def>
              <amount>28</amount>
            </li>
          </extraMeleeDamages>
        </surpriseAttack>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>right claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>16</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.5</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontRightPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <surpriseAttack>
          <extraMeleeDamages>
            <li>
              <def>Stun</def>
              <amount>28</amount>
            </li>
          </extraMeleeDamages>
        </surpriseAttack>
      </li>
      <li>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>19</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.85</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <surpriseAttack>
          <extraMeleeDamages>
            <li>
              <def>Stun</def>
              <amount>22</amount>
            </li>
          </extraMeleeDamages>
        </surpriseAttack>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>head</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>9</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.75</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.2</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <comps>
      <!-- MECHANIC 2: the egg-trap clutch. -->
      <li Class="CompProperties_EggLayer">
        <eggUnfertilizedDef>RSW_DrazzikEggUnfertilized</eggUnfertilizedDef>
        <eggFertilizedDef>RSW_DrazzikEggFertilized</eggFertilizedDef>
        <eggFertilizationCountMax>1</eggFertilizationCountMax>
        <eggLayIntervalDays>20</eggLayIntervalDays>
        <eggProgressUnfertilizedMax>0.5</eggProgressUnfertilizedMax>
        <eggCountRange>1~2</eggCountRange>
      </li>
      <!-- MECHANIC 1: the vibration lure. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_CompProperties_DrumLure">
        <luredHediff>RM_DrumLureLured</luredHediff>
        <submersionHediff>RM_DrumLureSubmersion</submersionHediff>
        <lureRadiusCells>18</lureRadiusCells>
        <ambushRangeCells>1.9</ambushRangeCells>
        <lureChancePerScan>0.35</lureChancePerScan>
        <checkIntervalTicks>90</checkIntervalTicks>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail</body>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <predator>true</predator>
      <baseBodySize>2.2</baseBodySize>
      <baseHungerRate>0.3</baseHungerRate>
      <baseHealthScale>2.3</baseHealthScale>
      <leatherDef>Leather_Panthera</leatherDef>
      <useMeatFrom>Cougar</useMeatFrom>
      <trainability>Advanced</trainability>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0.2</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>1</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <gestationPeriodDays>12</gestationPeriodDays>
      <foodType>CarnivoreAnimal, OvivoreAnimal</foodType>
      <lifeExpectancy>20</lifeExpectancy>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.25</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.5</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalFighter</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RSW_Drazzik</defName>
    <label>drazzik</label>
    <race>RSW_Drazzik</race>
    <combatPower>340</combatPower>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.05</ecoSystemWeight>
    <wildGroupSize>1~1</wildGroupSize>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <label>drazzik cub</label>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <!-- TEMP PLACEHOLDER: RSW_SandLion's own donor texture, bone/dust
               tinted so the shared silhouette still reads distinct. -->
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/AA_SandLion/AA_SandLion</texPath>
          <color>(222,214,196)</color>
          <drawSize>1.2</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/AA_SandLion/AA_Dessicated_SandLion</texPath>
          <drawSize>1.2</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>drazzik juvenile</label>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/AA_SandLion/AA_SandLion</texPath>
          <color>(222,214,196)</color>
          <drawSize>1.85</drawSize>
          <shadowData>
            <volume>(0.3, 0.3, 0.3)</volume>
            <offset>(0,0,-0.3)</offset>
          </shadowData>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/AA_SandLion/AA_Dessicated_SandLion</texPath>
          <drawSize>1.85</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/AA_SandLion/AA_SandLion</texPath>
          <color>(222,214,196)</color>
          <drawSize>2.5</drawSize>
          <shadowData>
            <volume>(0.4, 0.4, 0.4)</volume>
            <offset>(0,0,-0.1)</offset>
          </shadowData>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/AA_SandLion/AA_Dessicated_SandLion</texPath>
          <drawSize>2.5</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!-- The egg-trap clutch. "A large egg is portable water in a rigid shell,
       which is exactly why a Jawa prizes one... Some eggs are birth traps.
       Approached, they hatch violently, and the newborn tries to drink the
       intruder as fast as it can with sharp beaks and needle claws. The
       clutch is bait; the mother invested water in a weapon, not only in
       offspring." (deep_desert.md §4) -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="EggFertBase">
    <defName>RSW_DrazzikEggFertilized</defName>
    <label>drazzik egg</label>
    <description>Heavy for its size and cool to the touch, sloshing faintly when moved — everything a canteen-egg should feel like to a hand that has learned to trust that weight. Do not trust this one. Something is already moving inside, and it did not wait for the mother to leave before it started deciding who counts as prey.</description>
    <possessionCount>1</possessionCount>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>swresource/EggScaled</texPath>
      <color>(232,222,198)</color>
      <drawSize>0.85</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>35.0</MarketValue>
      <Mass>1.2</Mass>
      <Nutrition>0.55</Nutrition>
    </statBases>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Hatcher">
        <hatcherDaystoHatch>6</hatcherDaystoHatch>
        <hatcherPawn>RSW_Nizzek</hatcherPawn>
      </li>
      <!-- The trap: hatches early the moment something living gets close,
           rather than waiting out the vanilla timer above. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.ProximityHatch.CompProperties_ProximityHatch" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.proximityhatch">
        <triggerRadius>1.5</triggerRadius>
        <scanIntervalTicks>60</scanIntervalTicks>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="EggUnfertBase">
    <defName>RSW_DrazzikEggUnfertilized</defName>
    <label>drazzik egg (unfert.)</label>
    <description>Heavy for its size and cool to the touch, sloshing faintly when moved. Nothing is going to hatch out of this one — it is exactly what it feels like, a rigid shell of good water.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>swresource/EggScaled</texPath>
      <color>(232,222,198)</color>
      <drawSize>0.85</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>35.0</MarketValue>
      <Mass>1.2</Mass>
      <Nutrition>0.55</Nutrition>
    </statBases>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
